<title>MEXICO: Banamex asks to form Mexican AFORE.</title>
<headline>Banamex asks to form Mexican AFORE.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's largest bank, Banamex, said on Thursday that it had formally asked for authorisation to form an AFORE, one of the private pension funds set to come into effect in mid-1997.</p>
<p>&quot;We have complied with one of the main requirements, which is to make a formal demand for the constitution of the AFORE-Banamex,&quot; said the company in a statement.</p>
<p>The bank added that it also supported the Mexican government's decision, announced at the start of the week, to postpone for six months the start-up date of the AFOREs.</p>
<p>The private pension funds were originally scheduled to start on January 1 next year.</p>
<p>-- Mexico City newsroom (525) 728 9559</p>
